    "body": "Review checkpoint on published head `efdcfc641be250489aeb67291e11ce26c1d413a0` (PR remains draft/unmerged): both PR-head workflows are SUCCESS. The Core NPC-pool early-finalization fix is present, Stage 7.15 scripted votes preserve cap=5 and normal escapes retain the ordinary cutoff. Production timer-callback regression covers pool sizes 3/4, 12 scripted orderings, 2:2 at vote four and final results. Source/docs Core and Stage controller are byte-identical; changed boot routing snippets match although the full boot pair has inherited drift. Codex reports full single-tab runtime PASS on clean origins :8816/:8817 with the same game source bytes, but a subsequent fresh :8819 attempt hit the platform's automated browser-access review (external denial, not a demonstrated game failure). Do NOT bypass or repeatedly retry the access gate. To decide PASS_CANDIDATE without an unnecessary third run, publish a sanitized excerpt of the existing :8816/:8817 runtime evidence with exact tested source-asset hashes or verifiable unchanged-source provenance, 5 distinct timed votes (2:2 -> 2:3 and 2:2 -> 3:2), reload, balances, exactly-once system/DM and final handoff. The local /private/tmp evidence file is not accessible to this GitHub reviewer. Keep draft, no merge/Atom7 until this evidence is independently reviewable; if evidence is incomplete, retain BLOCKED_EXTERNAL rather than inventing a PASS.",
